It ports the Anecdoctor misinformation-elicitation technique as implemented in
Microsoft PyRIT (the Python Risk Identification Tool, https://github.com/microsoft/PyRIT),
pinned at commit 2016c4a8566bd66253d431ff38400bade4c77fa3. PyRIT is redistributed
under the MIT License (Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation); the upstream license
text is preserved verbatim in LICENSES/PyRIT-MIT.txt.

The technique is credited to its authors:

  Alejandro Cuevas, Saloni Dash, Bharat Kumar Nayak, Dan Vann, and
  Madeleine I. G. Daepp. "Anecdoctoring: Automated Red-Teaming Across Language
  and Place." Proceedings of the 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in
  Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2025), Microsoft Research.
  arXiv:2509.19143 — https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19143
  Published: https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.964/

