Bundled material (vendored byte-for-byte; sha256-pinned in _vendor/SHA256SUMS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Anecdoctor prompt templates, vendored verbatim from PyRIT:

- src/anecdoctor_optimizer/_vendor/pyrit/datasets/executors/anecdoctor/anecdoctor_build_knowledge_graph.yaml
- src/anecdoctor_optimizer/_vendor/pyrit/datasets/executors/anecdoctor/anecdoctor_use_fewshot.yaml
- src/anecdoctor_optimizer/_vendor/pyrit/datasets/executors/anecdoctor/anecdoctor_use_knowledge_graph.yaml

License: MIT (Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation). Prompt authorship metadata in
the vendored files additionally credits Saloni Dash, Alejandro Cuevas Villalba,
Bharat Kumar Nayak, Dayenne Souza, Dan Vann, and Madeleine Daepp (Microsoft
Research).

The Anecdoctor control flow (knowledge-graph build, few-shot framing, and
single framed-request emission) is reimplemented from scratch against superred's
async event model in src/anecdoctor_optimizer/ (original to this module, MIT). No
prompt/template body is reproduced in authored code.

